                            <a name="comment4213"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Versimilitude
</h4>

<p>
"It's factual for the more part - I'll give it that. But it's decribed in such a way as to lead readers into a different perception than what really exists."<br />
This is nonsense. <br />
No perception can exist outside the mind of the perceiver. If what you're saying is that your perception of the groves is different from Preston's, that's fair but largely irrelevant. If you're saying that Preston's description does not match reality, then how can you say he's "factual"? <br />
This is an example of how sloppy thought leads to sloppy writing. 
</p>
<div class="posted">Posted by:


		<a href="mailto:bmarvel@mindspring.com">Bill M.</a>
	

 at August 22,2008 09:21
</div>
